// Design 256 — a receiver whose type NAME is not bound in this file at all
// keeps its overload set. The value arrived through `hand()` and only `hand` is
// imported, so nothing here spells `Crate`; the set is keyed on the resolved
// type identity, and both scoping rules already put the whole extension surface
// in scope (the selective import makes the module a DIRECT import, and the
// receiver's inherent API travels with the value).
//
// DF-280a's third face, hit in the wild by sawos (Aug 31): the name-keyed
// re-resolution missed, every overload but the first-registered one went away,
// and `make(top: 1)` was "missing argument for parameter `entry`". The
// workaround was importing `Crate`, a name this file never writes —
// DF-247b's phantom-dependency shape.
// EXPECT: success
// EXPECT-OUTPUT: 8

import modules.overload280_dep.{hand}

func main() {
    let c = hand()
    print("{}", c.make(top: 1))
}
